# Byte-exact comparisons run in this repo (templates/*, the AGENTS.md block,
# and specs.md's fenced code blocks are diffed byte-for-byte against each
# other in test/templates.test.js) so every text file must check out with the
# same bytes on every platform. `text=auto eol=lf` normalizes line endings to
# LF in the working tree on all platforms and stores LF in the repo, which is
# simpler and safer than enumerating "contractual" files: that list has
# already proven easy to under-specify (specs.md itself is the oracle for the
# template comparisons and is easy to forget when hand-picking paths), and
# under-specifying it silently reintroduces the exact bug this file exists to
# prevent — CRLF written into a board that gets committed and shared with a
# Linux machine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touched by line-ending conversion, but declared
# explicitly so git's heuristic detection is never the only thing preventing
# corruption.
*.png binary
